hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2814","**\nNarrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, who said: Ashhab informed us, on the authority of Malik, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, on the authority of Salim ibn 'Abdullah, who said:\n\n'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan wrote to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf commanding him not to oppose Ibn 'Umar in matters of Hajj. When the Day of 'Arafah came, Ibn 'Umar came to him at the time when the sun had passed its zenith, and I was with him. He shouted near Saraqah, \Where is he?\"" So al-Hajjaj came out to him"","" wearing a cloak. He said to him"","" \""What is the matter"","" O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?\"" He said"","" \""Proceed to 'Arafah if you wish to follow the Sunnah.\""\n\nAl-Hajjaj said"","" \""Let me perform wudu' and drink some water"","" then I will come out to you.\"" So he waited for him until he came out"","" and then he walked between me and Abu [Salim]. I said to him"","" \""If you wish to follow the Sunnah"","" shorten the sermon and hasten to stand at 'Arafah.\"" He began to look at Ibn 'Umar to hear this from him. When Ibn 'Umar saw that"","" he said"","" \""He has spoken the truth.\""\n\n---"""""
